BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Woodworking Level 2 July 28 [Tuesdays - 6 week Comprehensive]
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260728T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260728T130000
UID:ttl-11006690820289@ttlmarket.com
DESCRIPTION:Woodworking Level 2 at TTLMakerspace\n\n \n \n Note: This cour
 se requires previous completion of Intro to Woodworking\n\n In this course
  at TTLMakerspace\, you will use and expand upon the skills learned in Int
 ro Woodworking. Working in a small group with dedicated instructor\, you'l
 l expand your skills in two practical box-building projects designed to de
 velop deeper understanding of woodworking.\n\n Build up confidence in the 
 shop and learn new\, valuable woodworking techniques.\n\n \n Materials and
  equipment for all projects are provided with the course. \n\n \n\n Schedu
 le : \n\n Six three-hour weekly classes\, Tuesdays 10am to 1pm. \n\n Outco
 mes : \n\n At the end of this course you will have achieved the following 
 goals: \n\n \n- Become more comfortable milling rough lumber \n\n- Complet
 e mitered corners \n\n- Complete box joints \n\n- Use a spline jig \n\n- C
 omplete inlays \n\n- Install hinges \n\n- Apply finishes \n\n- Learn how t
 o plan projects efficiently with minimal waste \n\n \n Following this cour
 se\, you'll be certified to use the woodshop. And you'll be able to join t
 he growing community of TTL Makers sharing knowledge on our Discord commun
 ity.\n\nUseful for: furniture\, cabinets\, organisers\, cutting-boards \n 
 \n \n \n Want to get notified next time classes are posted? \n\n Join our 
 mailing list!
LOCATION:TTLMakerspace\, 192 Spadina Ave.\, Toronto\, ON
URL:https://ttlmarket.com/products/woodworking-level-2-july-28-tuesdays-6-
 week-comprehensive
X-SOURCE:Toronto Tool Library
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Practical 3D Print Aug 3 [Mondays - 6 Week Comprehensive]
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260803T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260803T210000
UID:ttl-11006655398081@ttlmarket.com
DESCRIPTION:In this course at TTLMakerspace\, you will go beyond basic 3D 
 printing knowledge and be able to create custom designs. Learn to use CAD 
 modelling to upgrade or build your own models\, optimized for 3D print.\n\
 n \n \n \n \n \n \n Starting with manual printer control\, you will progre
 ss to custom modelling and even advanced techniques such as 3D scanning an
 d reverse engineering.\n\n Schedule: \n\n \n Six three-hour weekly classes
 \, Mondays 6:00pm to 9:00pm.\n\n \n \n \n \n \n Outcomes: \n \n \n At the 
 end of this course you will have achieved the following goals: \n \n \n \n
 - A complete understanding of the steps needed to go from concept to compl
 eted part\n\n- Experience and comprehension of parametric 3D modelling\n\n
 - Knowledge of 3D printing best practices \n\n- Familiarity with scanning
  for 3D print \n\n- Principles of reverse engineering and part repair\n\n
 - Understanding of the properties of different 3D printing filaments\n\n- 
 Use cases for SLA (resin) printing vs. FDM printing \n\n \n \n \n \n \n \
 n \n Following this hands-on course\, you’ll be certified to use 3D prin
 ters and book time with the machines at the TTLMakerspace (with your membe
 rship). You will also be able to join the growing community of TTL Makers 
 sharing 3D printing & 3D modelling knowledge on our Discord community.\n\n
  Useful for: design prototyping\, custom organizational tools\, repairs\, 
 prop-making\, decorations\, fabrication tools\n\n \n \n \n \n \n \n\n \n \
 n Want to get notified next time classes are posted? \n\n Join our mailing
  list!
LOCATION:TTLMakerspace\, 192 Spadina Ave.\, Toronto\, ON
URL:https://ttlmarket.com/products/practical-3d-print-aug-3-mondays-6-week
 -comprehensive
X-SOURCE:Toronto Tool Library
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:In Depth Sewing Intro - Aug 3 [Mondays - 6 week program]
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260803T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260803T210000
UID:ttl-11006643273921@ttlmarket.com
DESCRIPTION:LEARN TO SEW \n \n \n \n \n \n \n Suitable for beginners. This
  class goes over the basics of operating a sewing machine\, cutting and se
 wing garments\, and basic pattern alterations. \n \n \n The main project f
 or this class is an apron custom fit to YOU. A typical first project is a 
 tote bag\,but we’ve chosen to have our students make an apron as it cove
 rs the same skills while also teaching basic tailoring and fitting. The go
 al of this class is to provide students with the basic skills associated w
 ith sewing\, understanding patterns\, and textiles\, while promoting confi
 dence and shifting the mindset of your everyday clothing as things that su
 it your needs and body\, rather than things to simply wear. \n \n \n \n \n
  \n\n \n \n This class will also explore clothing repairs and minor altera
 tions like hemming\, altering\nnecklines\, adding pockets\, etc. Students 
 are encouraged to bring in items they wish to alter or repair. \n \n \n M
 aterials and equipment for all projects are provided with the course. \n \
 n \n\n \n Schedule \n6 weeks\, Mondays 6pm to 9pm \n \n \n\n \n \n Outcome
 s \n At the end of the course you will have achieved the following goals: 
 \n \n \n- Proficiency with operating a sewing machine safely \n\n- Underst
 anding of fabric types\, their uses\, how to prep them for sewing\, and ho
 w to cut fabric \n\n- Comfort with taking measurements of the body and how
  to apply them to a pattern \n\n- Knowledge of basic pattern alterations a
 nd how to adjust existing garments to fit you better \n\n- Understanding o
 f how to transfer patterns to fabric so that space is used as efficiently 
 as possible \n\n- Understanding of pinning and ironing techniques \n\n- Fa
 miliarity with basic sewing techniques including seams\, hemming\, hand st
 itching\,\napplying pockets\, fasteners including buttons\, zippers\, snap
 s\, and ties\, as well as\ndifferent stitch uses for different techniques 
 and materials\n\n- Basic repairs like fixing holes\, torn seams\, holes in
  pockets\, adding patches\n\n- Basic alterations like adjusting hems\, cha
 nging necklines\, switching out buttons or other fasteners
LOCATION:TTLMakerspace\, 192 Spadina Ave.\, Toronto\, ON
URL:https://ttlmarket.com/products/in-depth-sewing-intro-aug-3-mondays-6-w
 eek-program
X-SOURCE:Toronto Tool Library
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
