UID:ttl-11006631641281@ttlmarket.com
DESCRIPTION:Description: \n\n \n Suitable for beginners\, this woodworkin
 g course is designed to teach you all that you need to get started in wood
 working by learning both traditional\, and modern techniques.\n\n Students
  will learn valuable hands-on skills working on instructor-lead projects u
 sing both hand and power tools.\n\n Projects are chosen to provide skills 
 development in a natural progression from familiarity with the unique char
 acteristics of wood\, to basic essential techniques\, to some more advance
 d topics.\n\n Materials and equipment for all projects are provided with t
 he course.\n\n \n\n Schedule : \n\n Six three-hour weekly classes\, Sunda
 ys 10am to 1pm. \n\n Outcomes : \n\n At the end of this course you will ha
 ve achieved the following goals: \n\n \n- A complete understanding of the 
 nature and properties of wood \n\n- Proficiency with traditional woodworki
 ng techniques\n\n- Comfort working with chisels\, planes\, saws\n\n- Profi
 ciency with wood milling techniques\n\n- Comfort with safe operation of p
 ower tools\n\n- Familiarity with power planing\, joiner\, drill press\, ro
 uter and table saw \n\n- Dressing and laminating wood \n\n- Experience fo
 llowing project plans \n\n- Familiarity with joinery \n\n- Wood finishing\
 , various treatments \n\n \n  Following this course\, you'll be certified
  to use the woodshop. And you'll be able to join the growing community of 
 TTL Makers sharing knowledge on our Discord community.\n\n Certifications 
 for all courses are valid for one year from the time that they are issued\
 , and can be renewed at no cost with your active monthly membership within
  3 months of their expiry. Certification renewal requires booking with an 
 instructor\, is conducted at the makerspace\, and helps you keep your skil
 ls current. \n\nUseful for: furniture\, cabinets\, organisers\, cutting-b
 oards \n \n \n \n Want to get notified next time classes are posted? \n\n 
 Join our mailing list!
LOCATION:TTLMakerspace\, 192 Spadina Ave.\, Toronto\, ON
URL:https://ttlmarket.com/products/in-depth-intro-to-woodworking-aug-9-sun
 days-6-week-intensive
X-SOURCE:Toronto Tool Library
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Designing for Lasers - July 11 [Saturdays 6 week comprehensive]
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260711T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260711T170000
UID:ttl-11006618206401@ttlmarket.com
DESCRIPTION:In this course at TTLMakerspace\, you will go from beginner to
  practical working knowledge of designing and modelling in 2D and 3D\, and
  the operation of a laser for etching and cutting a variety of materials. 
 \n\n Starting with desktop versions of lasers you’ll work your way throu
 gh lessons and projects up to the industrial ThunderLaser cutter. \n\n Out
 comes: \n\n At the end of this course you will have achieved the following
  goals: \n\n \n- A complete understanding of the steps needed to go from c
 oncept to completed project \n\n- Familiarity with the properties of a var
 iety of materials - woods\, plastics\, textiles \n\n- Experience and compr
 ehension of the most important principles of CAD modelling for constructin
 g with laser cut parts \n\n- Setting speeds and power levels \n\n- Creatin
 g a design environment and workflow \n\n- Full understanding of the most c
 ommon etching and cutting operations \n\n- Experience creating tool paths 
 with Lightburn software \n\n- Setting up materials and performing operatio
 ns \n\n- Machine maintenance and Safety \n\n \n Schedule: 6 lessons\, Satu
 rdays\, 2pm-5pm \n\n Following this course\, you’ll be certified to use 
 desktop lasers\, and book time with the industrial laser at TTLMakerspace 
 (with your membership). You will also be able to join the growing communit
 y of TTL Makers sharing Laser knowledge on our Discord community. \n\n Use
 ful for : signs\, gifts\, personalising anything\, stamp-making\, organise
 r\, decorative items\, lanterns \n\n Want to get notified next time classe
 s are posted? \n\n Join our mailing list!
LOCATION:TTLMakerspace\, 192 Spadina Ave.\, Toronto\, ON
URL:https://ttlmarket.com/products/designing-for-lasers-july-11-saturdays-
 6-week-comprehensive
X-SOURCE:Toronto Tool Library
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Game Design Comprehensive Aug 4 [6 weeks\, Tuesdays]
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260804T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260804T210000
UID:ttl-11006607327425@ttlmarket.com
DESCRIPTION:Game Design Quick-start \n\n In this course at TTLMakerspace\,
  you will go from beginner to a working knowledge of game design and devel
 opment using the open-source engine Godot. \n\n Starting with the basics o
 f the game engine\, you’ll learn how to progress from a knowledge of gam
 e mechanics to a coherent\, engaging game experience. \n\n \n \n \n Worksh
 op Schedule : \n Mondays\, 6pm to 9pm (3 hours) \n \n \n \n \n \n Outcomes
  : \n \n \n \n \n At the end of this course you will have achieved the fol
 lowing goals: \n\n \n- \n A grasp of planning out fun game-play mechanics 
 \n\n- \n Familiarity with features of the Godot Game Engine \n\n- \n Pract
 ical knowledge of animation techniques \n\n- \n Application of physics for
  game-play mechanics \n\n- \n Comfort with 2D game development \n\n- \n Ab
 ility to publish and show your game \n\n- \n Working understanding of UI i
 n games \n\n \n Following this course\, you’ll be welcome to join the gr
 owing community of creators and game developers at TTLMakerspace for conti
 nued support and encouragement in your game development journey. \n\n \n \
 n \n Useful for: games\, art\, installations\, animation\, interactive exp
 eriences \n \n \n \n \n Want to get notified next time classes are posted?
   \n\n Join our mailing list!
LOCATION:TTLMakerspace\, 192 Spadina Ave.\, Toronto\, ON
URL:https://ttlmarket.com/products/game-design-comprehensive-aug-4-6-weeks
 -tuesdays
X-SOURCE:Toronto Tool Library
