UID:ttl-10932864319681@ttlmarket.com
DESCRIPTION:Music Makers \n\n \n \n Recommended Ages 8-13 \n \n \n\n \n \n
  \n \n\n \n For a whole week we will study\, design and build various type
 s of musical instruments. With a heavy emphasis on safety\, we will empowe
 r kids with the confidence and skills needed to use tools and equipment in
  a community makerspace.\n\n \n Every day we will select a type of musical
  instrument. We will learn its history and construction methods before des
 igning and building one of our own. We will end the week with a Jam Sessio
 n that parents are encouraged to spectate.\n\n \n Instrument Design\, Soun
 d Theory using leatherworking tools\, hand tools\, power tools\, laser cut
 ting and 3d printing.\n\n \n \n Note: Instruments can be taken home. TTL t
 eaches kids to reduce\, re-use\, and recycle parts into new projects!\n\n 
 \n \n \n \n \n\n \n \n Day 1 - Monday \n \n \n \n \n Morning - Ocarina - 3
 D printing.\n\n We will be exploring the world of 3d printing with a lesso
 n on how 3d printers work\, how slicing is done and different materials an
 d tricks to create our first working musical instrument.\n\n Afternoon –
  Study of the history of music and musical instruments. Design time.\n\n \
 n \n \n \n \n \n Day 2 - Tuesday \n \n \n \n \n Wooden Xylophone – Woodw
 orking\n\n We start with a shop safety orientation. The kids will select p
 lanks\, mill\, cut\, drill and sand the pieces they need to assemble a pla
 yable and hopefully tuned instrument by the end of the day.\n\n \n \n \n \
 n \n \n Day 3 - Wednesday \n \n \n \n \n Stringed instruments – Laser cu
 tting. Woodworking\n\n We will use the precision and speed of the shop las
 ers to invent and create a stringed instrument.\n\n special attention will
  be given to the acoustic chamber.\n\n \n \n \n \n \n \n Day 4 - Thursday 
 \n \n \n \n \n Drums – Woodworking and Leatherworking\n\n We will study 
 different types of drums\, select a design and create a drum with a skin a
 nd a cajon. We may experiment with drumsticks if we have time in the after
 noon.\n\n \n \n \n \n \n \n\n \n \n Day 5  - Friday \n \n \n \n \n \n Mor
 ning - Shakers - 3d Printing\, Laser cutting and Woodworking.\n\n Using th
 e variety of different tools and techniques learned this week the kids wil
 l be encouraged to make a shaker or morracas of sorts.\n\n \n \n \n \n \n 
 \n\n \n About Kids Camps at TTLMakerspace \n \n \n We love our young maker
 s at TTLMakerspace\, and run kids programs all year long for our active me
 mbers. Our summer camps provide the opportunity for curious young builders
  to have a very hands-on experience mastering tools both traditional and h
 igh-tech. \n \n \n\n \n Schedule \n \n \n \n\n \n Drop off 8:45 to 9:00 am
  \n \n \n 9:15  am  skill training \n \n \n 10:30 am  Break and Snacks 
 \n \n \n 10:45 am  Building Session 1 \n \n \n 12:00 pm  Lunch (At the G
 range Park weather permitting) Kids will be required to bring a lunch and 
 we recommend a re-usable water bottle that they can refill during the week
 . \n \n \n 1:00  pm  Building Session 2 \n \n \n 2:30  pm  Break and S
 nacks \n \n \n 2:45  pm  Building Session 3 \n \n \n 3:45  pm Cleaning 
 \n \n \n Pick up 4:00 to 4:15 pm with extended care available for an addit
 ional fee.
